// push-batch-policy.mjs (12 October 2026): ONE definition of how uploaded data is grouped into git pushes.
//
// EN: Every number lives in the single configuration object built by loadPushPolicyConfig (HDA rule: one definition, one
//     parameter interface, environment overrides, a bad value raises an error that names the parameter). The planning functions
//     are pure; the controller is a small state machine; the engine runPushBatch drives ONE batch to a confirmed push.
// FR : tous les nombres vivent dans un seul objet de configuration ; les fonctions de plan sont pures, le controleur est une
//     petite machine a etats, le moteur runPushBatch mene UN lot jusqu'a une poussee confirmee.
//
// DECISIONS OF MATTHIEU (12 October 2026, final):
//   D1 Target 1 900 MiB per push = 20 parts of 95 MiB (each part is 95 MiB + 16 bytes of AES-GCM tag), 7.2 % under the ENFORCED
//      2 GiB (2 048 MiB) per push of GitHub. Fill each batch to the maximum, never above the safety threshold. A failure is
//      counted PER BATCH: one failure is retried unchanged (network, timeout and GitHub server errors can be accidental), the
//      THIRD failure of the same batch falls back to the OLD RULE (2 parts = 190 MiB), then the policy recovers step by step
//      after 3 consecutive successes. Ladder [2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20] parts, start at 20 (14 October 2026), never above 20.
//   D2 Archive repository cap 4 096 MiB (was 2 GiB): 43 parts per repository instead of 21, about half the repository
//      creations (the creations are what trigger the secondary rate limit 403 waves). Applies to NEW films only: a manifest
//      stores the repository inside every part url, the part index is never mapped back to a repository at read time.
//      Evidence: an old note (10 June 2026, scripts/_archive/eagle-video-bulk.mjs:37) reports pushes that bring a repository to
//      about 4 GB rejected in series; on 12 October 2026 the GitHub API `size` shows repositories of 9.7 to 10.4 GB accepting
//      pushes (zenray-vid-public-31, zenray-vid-public-32, zenrayshards-vid-36499389363f). A rejection at the cap boundary is
//      still classified permanent and fails cleanly (no data loss, the part files stay in the clone, the caller moves to a new
//      repository).
//
// WHAT IS NOT DECIDED HERE: how the data is staged. The callers (video-raw-lib, video-git-shard) stage, commit and push; this
// module only decides how many items go in the next push and what to do when it fails.

